Web source  : web/src/features/telemetry/pages/SignalGapDetectorPage.tsx
Output      : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/SignalGapDetectorPage/ (+ NavigationView registration, test, resw, ledger)
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300), maui-windows workload installed — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  SignalLogViewerPage / SignalsWorkspacePage do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "TeslaSync/Features/Telemetry/SignalGapDetectorPage.xaml + SignalGapDetectorPageViewModel.cs" is mapped onto
  these real conventions (namespace TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Telemetry, aligning with RouteGroup.TelemetrySignals).
- Faithful scope (no scope narrowing, no stubs — ADR-011): the web SignalGapDetectorPage is a thin wrapper that
  renders a header (title/subtitle + VehicleSelect), the no-vehicle EmptyState (web `!vehicleId || vehicleId<=0`),
  and otherwise the shared <SignalCatalogPanel vehicleId=…>. The native port reproduces ALL of these regions: the
  header, the parity-tracked no-vehicle empty state, AND a complete native catalog (the SignalCatalogPanel port:
  the four summary StatCards, the search box, the tri-state filter (All/Stale Only/Active Only) and tri-state sort
  (Most Stale/A-Z/Category) toggles, and the staleness table — status band, signal, last value, last updated, time
  since) with its own loading / empty / error states. The manifest scopes this unit's PARITY_REQUIRED to the empty
  state + four chrome strings (it has no API data sources of its own — the catalog data source belongs to the shared
  SignalCatalogPanel), but the catalog region is still rendered in full so the vehicle-selected branch is never a
  stub.
- Data binding (ADR-004): SignalGapDetectorClientFeed binds the page's two web data sources to the generated
  OpenAPI contract client — GET /vehicles (web useSelectedVehicle, op get_api_v1_vehicles) and
  GET /signals/{vehicleID}/live (web useSignalGaps, op get_api_v1_signals_vehicleID_live, verified present in
  Generated/Api/ApiEndpoints.cs). The default EmptySignalGapDetectorFeed keeps the shell-registered page mountable
  without a backend (resolves the no-vehicle empty state, no HTTP). No HTTP touches the view; every payload
  round-trips through the tolerant SignalGapDetectorVehicle.ParseList / SignalGapLiveEntry.ParseLive parsers.
- Data states (manifest declares state=empty; the catalog source adds loading/empty/error/success): the page union
  is SignalGapDetectorState {Loading (initial fleet fetch), Empty (no vehicle — the parity empty state), Error
  (fleet fetch failed → failure banner), Catalog (vehicle selected)}; the catalog union is SignalGapCatalogState
  {Loading (TsTableSkeleton), Error (inline danger banner), Empty (web "No signal data available"), Success}. No
  region is ever hidden behind a null (ADR-011): a vehicle with zero signals shows the friendly empty state, a
  search/filter with no matches keeps the table with the web "No signals match current filters" message.
- Staleness is recomputed at the display boundary against `now` (web recomputes on every refresh): StalenessSeconds
  / CategoryOf (never / stale>300s / active) / BandOf (never / active<30s / aging<300s / stale) port
  getCatalogStalenessStyle + the web SignalRow.category exactly; FormatStaleness ports formatStaleness
  (Ns ago / Nm ago / Nh Nm ago); the summary counts (total / active / stale / never) port the web reducers.
- Panels (ADR-005), in web source order: the summary StatCard grid (TsStatCard ×4), the controls panel
  (TsGlassPanel: TsInput search + filter TsButtons + sort TsButtons + the "Refreshes every 5s" caption), and the
  catalog body (TsTableSkeleton / TsAlertBanner / TsDataTable Selectable=false / TsEmptyState / last-refreshed
  caption). No hardcoded colours/typography — PageTitle/Subhead/Caption + TsStatCard/TsBadge/TsButton + the W1
  design tokens drive light/dark/high-contrast.
- Navigation entry: RouteTable.cs ALREADY maps Page("SignalGapDetector","signal-gaps",RouteGroup.TelemetrySignals,
  "Signal Gaps") — unchanged. ShellWindow.xaml.cs registers the page factory
  (_viewModel.PageFactory.Register("SignalGapDetector", () => new FeatureViews.Telemetry.SignalGapDetectorPage())).
  This page introduces NO new route surface.
- i18n (ADR-014): every visible literal resolves through ILocalizer.GetString(key, englishFallback) using the exact
  web key names (signalGap.title/subtitle/noVehicle/noVehicleDesc + the shared catalog keys
  filterPlaceholder/filterLabel/status/category/refreshInterval/noData/noMatch/totalSignals/active/stale/
  neverReceived/all/staleOnly/activeOnly/mostStale/az/signal/lastValue/lastUpdated/timeSince/lastRefreshed). The
  Windows catalog Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw is AUTO-GENERATED by apps/shared/i18n/generators/gen-i18n.ts
  from apps/shared/i18n/catalog/*.json and is checksum/drift-gated (".gitattributes" pins it eol=lf for the
  gen-i18n -Check gate). The canonical catalog already carries translation.signalGap.title /
  translation.signalGap.subtitle (and the whole shared catalog-key set the catalog page reuses) but NOT
  signalGap.noVehicle / signalGap.noVehicleDesc — the web page itself supplies these via t(key, fallback) because
  the web i18n catalog has no entry for them either. Per the established sibling precedent (W7 StatusApiDocsPage /
  HelpPage), the generated resw is therefore NOT hand-edited (that would fail the gen-i18n drift gate); instead
  signalGap.noVehicle / signalGap.noVehicleDesc and the native-only status-band labels (web's hardcoded
  'Never received'/'Active'/'Aging'/'Stale', externalised under signalGap.band*) resolve through the verbatim
  English fallback on the ShellLocalizer → ResourceLoader bridge — exactly how the web renders them. Zero hardcoded
  UI text (every literal flows through one keyed GetString call site); the key names match web; the auto-generated
  catalog is left byte-for-byte untouched.
- a11y (ADR-015): AutomationProperties names on the page (title), the vehicle picker, the controls panel, each
  filter/sort toggle (its label) and each catalog row (signal + status + value + time-since); decorative glyphs set
  AccessibilityView=Raw; the failure banners are live regions; light/dark + high-contrast honoured through the W1
  tokens; ≥ minimum target sizes via the shared TsButton/TsSelect controls.
- Units (ADR-005 / P1-S5): the catalog renders telemetry signal values verbatim (the value column is the raw last
  value, not a measured quantity needing conversion) and freshness ages formatted at the display boundary; no
  non-SI value is stored or computed.

